From 50fd2c023c1a8cfee570c6aa6d48b6fcd6cbd74a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:32:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: mm: vmscan: force MGLRU fully enabled by default

On devices where init.rc writes 0 to /sys/kernel/mm/lru_gen/enabled
at boot and no persist.device_config.mglru_native trigger later
raises it, MGLRU never gets enabled without a manual write.

Force store_enabled() to always request all lru_gen_caps bits
(CORE, MM_WALK, NONLEAF_YOUNG) regardless of what was written, and
always call lru_gen_change_state(true) for CORE. Unsupported caps
are still dropped by the existing capability checks, same as a
manual `echo 7 > enabled` would do. Writes continue to return
success so init.rc's write does not surface an error.

Test: cat /sys/kernel/mm/lru_gen/enabled reads back the maximum
value supported by the running kernel/hardware after boot,
regardless of init.rc's write or DeviceConfig state.

Signed-off-by: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index 74a933fa0..ced168850 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -5887,11 +5887,14 @@ static ssize_t store_enabled(struct kobject *kobj, struct kobj_attribute *attr,
 	else if (kstrtouint(buf, 0, &caps))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* Force MGLRU on: request all caps, kernel caps to what's supported */
+	caps |= BIT(LRU_GEN_CORE) | BIT(LRU_GEN_MM_WALK) | BIT(LRU_GEN_NONLEAF_YOUNG);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < NR_LRU_GEN_CAPS; i++) {
 		bool enabled = caps & BIT(i);
 
 		if (i == LRU_GEN_CORE)
-			lru_gen_change_state(enabled);
+			lru_gen_change_state(true); /* always enable core */
 		else if (enabled)
 			static_branch_enable(&lru_gen_caps[i]);
 		else
-- 
2.55.0

